 $\\,0.2\\,$ | $\\,0.6064\\,$ | $\\,0.6103\\,$ | $\\,0.6141\\,$ |\n| $\\,0.3\\,$ | $\\,0.6443\\,$ | $\\,0.6480\\,$ | $\\,0.6517\\,$ |\n| $\\,0.4\\,$ | $\\,0.6808\\,$ | $\\,0.6844\\,$ | $\\,0.6879\\,$ |\n\n$P(Z<-0.38)=$\n{{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14069722/state.json" "file_sha256" "f38b28e68eb1c72046b151d63c599d8baf82ed4ee0a6819917072f7c857cf6bd"} {"question" "q-330661" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14069722/assets/8a6467813ccf982906fb5d1d8cd5c5c88b984c22a1e238715c65315a7772249c.png)\n\nFor a random variable $Z∼N(0,1),$ we have the following symmetry property for $a>0:$\n\n$$\nP(Z>a)=P(Z<-a)=Φ(-a)\n$$\n\nWe're given that $Z∼N(0,1),$ and we wish to compute $P(Z<-0.38).$ The required probability is represented by the area shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14069722/assets/ee2aebec9953a09dca6eab5c7e5434240885a383a6701638fffdaa9ee9cfeb40.png)\n\nBy symmetry, this equals the area corresponding to the probability $P(Z>0.38).$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14069722/assets/619fae52bde8b2da729095f733e1ea1411132fffe70cc23e252a83cbb2e7ff23.png)\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(Z<-0.38) & =P(Z>0.38) \\\\  & =1-P(Z<0.38) \\\\  & =1-Φ(0.38) \\\\  & =1-0.6480 \\\\  & =0.3520.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14069722/state.json" "file_sha256" "f38b28e68eb1c72046b151d63c599d8baf82ed4ee0a6819917072f7c857cf6bd"} {"question" "q-330661" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14069722/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "9675d4395