 the area shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14069722/assets/e708b9dc6927a17f193c216f1b14b1b9ef98e6d9d26a998790112863661ca5d0.png)\n\nBy symmetry, this equals the area corresponding to the probability $P(Z>-1.94).$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14069722/assets/43f1e2eb5354cbdcd5ff359985048fa2d6411167ad5f50fe45c730642e184b61.png)\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(Z<1.94) & =P(Z>-1.94) \\\\  & =1-P(Z<-1.94) \\\\  & =1-Φ(-1.94) \\\\  & =1-0.0262 \\\\  & =0.9738.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14069722/state.json" "file_sha256" "f38b28e68eb1c72046b151d63c599d8baf82ed4ee0a6819917072f7c857cf6bd"} {"question" "q-330651" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14069722/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "9675d43953465dc0c2310694be85278d058ad772405778d09e3fc4335832b01f"} {"question" "q-330651" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14069722/state.json" "file_sha256" "f38b28e68eb1c72046b151d63c599d8baf82ed4ee0a6819917072f7c857cf6bd"} {"question" "q-330651" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "0.9738"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14069722/state.json" "file_sha256" "f38b28e68eb1c72046b151d63c599d8baf82ed4ee0a6819917072f7c857cf6bd"} {"question" "q-183828" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "The data below is taken from the table of values of the cumulative distribution function $Φ(z)$ for the standard normal distribution. Given that $Z∼N(0,1),$ compute $P(-0.19<Z<0.38).$\n\n| $z$ | $\\,0.07\\,$ | $\\,0.08\\,$ | $\\,0.09\\,$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $\\,-0.3\\,$ | $\\,0.3557\\,$ | $\\,0.3520\\,$ | $\\,0.3483\\,$ |\n| $\\,-0.2\\,$ | $\\,0.3936\\,$ | $\\,0.3897\\,$ | $\\,0.3859\\,$ |\n| $\\,-0.1\\,$ | $\\,0.4325\\,$ | $\\,0.4286\\,$ | $\\,0.4247\\,$ |" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14069722/state.json" "file_sha256" "f38b28e68eb1c72046b151d63c599d8baf82ed4ee0a6819917072f7c857cf6bd"} {"question" "q-183828" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We're given that $Z∼N(0,1),$ and we wish to compute $P(-0.19<Z<0.38).$ The required probability is represented by the area shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14069722/assets/bd478e9925303e3d018e2d070e4e3a78e72fb699a48ac3109ddf743158bb5599.png)\n\nBy the definition of the cumulative distribution function $Φ(z),$ \n\n$$\nP(Z\\le z)=Φ(z).\n$$\n\nSo, we express the required probability in terms of $Φ(z)$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(-0.19<Z<0.38) & =P(Z<0.38)-P(Z\\le -0.19) \\\\  & =P(Z\\le 0.38)-P(Z\\le -0.19) \\\\  & =Φ(0.38)-Φ(-0.19)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the table, we know that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Φ(-0.38) & =0.3520 \\\\ Φ(-0.19) & =0.4247,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nbut we are not given $Φ(0.38).$ However, we can compute this using symmetry:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Φ(0.38) & =P(Z\\le 0.38) \\\\  & =P(Z\\ge -0.38) \\\\  & =1-P(Z<-0.38) \\\\  & =1-P(Z\\le -0.38) \\\\  & =1-Φ(-0.38) \\\\  & =1-0.3520 \\\\  & =0.6480\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(-0.19<Z<0.38) & =Φ(0.38)-Φ(-0.19) \\\\  & =0.6480-0.4247 \\\\  & =0.2233.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14069722/state.json" "file_sha256" "f38b28e68eb1c72046b151d63c599d8baf82ed4ee0a6819917072f7c857cf6bd"} {"question" "q-183