\\\\  & =Φ(1.54)-Φ(-1.54)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the table, we know that\n\n$$\nΦ(-1.54)=0.0618,\n$$\n\nbut we are not given $Φ(1.54).$ However, we can compute this using symmetry:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Φ(1.54) & =P(Z\\le 1.54) \\\\  & =1-P(Z\\le -1.54) \\\\  & =1-Φ(-1.54) \\\\  & =1-0.0618 \\\\  & =0.9382\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(-1.54<Z<1.54) & =Φ(1.54)-Φ(-1.54) \\\\  & =0.9382-0.0618 \\\\  & =0.8764.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14069722/state.json" "file_sha256" "f38b28e68eb1c72046b151d63c599d8baf82ed4ee0a6819917072f7c857cf6bd"} {"question" "q-330908" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14069722/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "9675d43953465dc0c2310694be85278d058ad772405778d09e3fc4335832b01f"} {"question" "q-330908" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14069722/state.json" "file_sha256" "f38b28e68eb1c72046b151d63c599d8baf82ed4ee0a6819917072f7c857cf6bd"} {"question" "q-330908" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "0.8764"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14069722/state.json" "file_sha256" "f38b28e68eb1c72046b151d63c599d8baf82ed4ee0a6819917072f7c857cf6bd"} {"question" "q-183823" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "The data below is taken from the table of values of the cumulative distribution function $Φ(z)$ for the standard normal distribution. Given that $Z∼N(0,1),$ compute $P(-0.18<Z<0.18).$\n\n| $z$ | $\\,0.06\\,$ | $\\,0.07\\,$ | $\\,0.08\\,$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|